tengine/godot/pull/110669.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/code_style.html\r\n-->\r\n### Adds move_and_push() functions to CharacterBody3D and CharacterBody2D.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\n#### Reason: There are situations where you want players to push objects as they collide.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  -  move_and_push() internally call move_and_slide() but applies an impulse to any rigid bodies that collides with the player\r\n\r\n  -  Scaling with multiplier variable and PhysicsMaterial bounce value\r\n\r\n  -  Adds collision multiplier to scale the impulse caused by the player\r\n\r\n  ~~-  Adds material presets to PhysicsMaterial~~\r\n\r\nBelow are examples of how move_and_slide work within Godot - followed up by the new move_and_push\r\n\r\n[2d example](https://youtu.be/wTOi8t6JIQg)\r\n\r\n[3d example](https://youtu.be/iLEmpQn1iks)\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is a code implementation to solve this proposal I made:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13211\r\n\r\nThis is an improved pull request of one I made previously:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110648\r\n\r\n* *Bugsquad edit, closes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13211*\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110669/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":3,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110669/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}